  "label": "a member joining an item with a diverging body is settled by the collection's prefer-incoming, reported Added, ContentChanged and Overruled",
  "note": "source a holds the card at c1; source b binds none of it and lists the same UID carrying c2. The member joins the item (SYNC.md §6) and its body is folded (§9): b holds no base, so b changed; the item's c1 differs from b's shared_object, none, falling back to its base, none, so the item changed for b; the two disagree. The collection's prefer-incoming adopts c2 and keeps c1, the body it replaced, as a retained item over b's handle. The join is reported Added, the adopted body ContentChanged and the kept one Overruled, in that order. b's base and shared_object are c2 at s1, so b owes nothing; a's base stays c1, so a owes c2 on its next sync",
